// =============================================================================
// Pattern B - per-user Claude token attribution (via APIM, streaming-safe)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT THIS DOES
//   Produces per-user prompt+completion tokens by joining APIM's native LLM token
//   log (ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog, SSE-aware) to the caller oid the policy
//   stamped as x-caller-oid, then prices it and reconciles the total.
//
//   SYSTEM OF RECORD = the native gateway LLM log. We do NOT read the streamed
//   response body in a policy - that breaks SSE (see 04-apim-policy.xml).
//
//   PROVIDES per user: prompt + completion tokens (streaming-safe).
//   DOES NOT provide per user: cache tokens. Cache is total-only reconciliation
//   against the Foundry Azure Monitor metrics (cacheReadInputTokens / ephemeral
//   5m/1h), which carry NO caller dimension.
//
// PREREQUISITES (from 05-enable-diagnostics.ps1)
//   - ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog enabled (token logging for LLM APIs).
//   - GatewayLogs capturing the x-caller-oid request header.
//   - Column names below may vary by API version - confirm against the live schema.
//
// PLACEHOLDERS TO FILL
//   The rate card in Q2 uses ILLUSTRATIVE list prices keyed by deployment name.
//   Replace <CLAUDE_SONNET_DEPLOYMENT> / <CLAUDE_OPUS_DEPLOYMENT> and the rates.
// =============================================================================

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q1. Per-user prompt+completion tokens: join LLM token log to the caller-oid header.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
let idByCorrelation =
    ApiManagementGatewayLogs
    | where isnotempty(CorrelationId)
    // x-caller-oid is surfaced in the captured request headers (exact column depends on the
    // diagnostic header-capture config; adjust to your schema, e.g. a RequestHeaders dynamic).
    | extend callerOid = tostring(parse_json(tostring(RequestHeaders))["x-caller-oid"])
    | where isnotempty(callerOid)
    | project CorrelationId, callerOid;

ApiManagementGatewayLlmLog
| project TimeGenerated, CorrelationId,
          model = tostring(DeploymentName),
          promptTokens = tolong(PromptTokens),
          completionTokens = tolong(CompletionTokens)
| join kind=leftouter idByCorrelation on CorrelationId
| summarize promptTokens = sum(promptTokens), completionTokens = sum(completionTokens), calls = count()
          by bin(TimeGenerated, 1d), callerOid = coalesce(callerOid, "unattributed"), model
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Q2. Per-user LIST-PRICE ESTIMATE (prompt+completion only). Label it an estimate.
//   Cache cost is NOT in here - it is reconciled at the resource level (Q3).
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
let rateCard = datatable(model:string, inputPerM:real, outputPerM:real)
[
    "<CLAUDE_SONNET_DEPLOYMENT>", 3.00, 15.00,   // ILLUSTRATIVE
    "<CLAUDE_OPUS_DEPLOYMENT>",  15.00, 75.00    // ILLUSTRATIVE
];
// (join Q1 output to rateCard on model and compute input*inputPerM/1e6 + output*outputPerM/1e6)

// =============================================================================
// Q3. RECONCILIATION. Compare SUM(per-user estimate) to the Azure Marketplace meter total for
//     the Claude resource in Cost Management, at resource x day. The gap is dominated by CACHE
//     tokens (not attributable per user here) plus streaming/estimation error. Report it as a
//     named residual owned by the platform team; allocate by token share only as a stated policy.
//     Foundry cache metrics (cacheReadInputTokens / ephemeral 5m/1h) reconcile the cache TOTAL,
//     not the person.
// =============================================================================

// Ops-only (NOT accounting): App Insights llm-emit-token-metric, bounded dimensions, capped at 100 values.
